Troubleshooting Tips
Elasticsearch won't start:

Check Java installation: java -version
Verify configuration: sudo nano /etc/elasticsearch/elasticsearch.yml
Check logs: sudo journalctl -u elasticsearch
Ensure sufficient memory (8GB minimum)
Logstash not processing logs:

Verify file permissions: ls -l /var/log/auth.log
Check Logstash logs: sudo journalctl -u logstash
Test configuration: sudo /usr/share/logstash/bin/logstash --config.test_and_exit -f /etc/logstash/conf.d/monitoring.conf
Restart service: sudo systemctl restart logstash
Kibana not accessible:

Verify Kibana is running: sudo systemctl status kibana
Check port availability: netstat -tulpn | grep 5601
Review logs: sudo journalctl -u kibana
Python scripts connection errors:

Verify Elasticsearch is accessible: curl localhost:9200
Check Python requests library: pip3 install requests
Validate JSON query syntax
Review script logs for detailed error messages
